<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<StyleSet xmlns="http://adamantium/ui"
          xmlns:x="http://adamantium/ui/xaml/extensions">

    <!-- Deliberately EMPTY, and it exists to say so.
         No default Foreground on TextBlock. Plain text takes this theme's primary colour by INHERITANCE from the window
         (see WindowStyleSet), never from a per-TextBlock setter. A Style-priority Foreground here would outrank the
         inherited value a control pushes onto its own content when its state changes - a selected row recolouring its
         text - so templated text could never follow selection, press or disabling. Inheritance lets the nearest
         ancestor win: the window's default reaches loose text, and a control overrides it inside itself.
         The file is here rather than absent because this theme owns an answer for every control, and "nothing, for
         this reason" is an answer. Without it the next person to notice that TextBlock has no style adds one. -->

</StyleSet>
